meta {
  name: Object with an image
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/v1/objects/:objectId
  body: none
  auth: none
}

params:path {
  objectId: 45734
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.body.objectID: eq 45734
  res.body.primaryImageSmall: startsWith https://images.metmuseum.org/
  res.body.isPublicDomain: eq true
  res.body.title: isString
}

docs {
  The record behind one tile ("Quail and Millet"). Objects are still on
  `v1`; there is no `v1.1/objects`.

  The gallery uses `primaryImageSmall`, `title`, `artistDisplayName` (or
  `culture` when there is no artist), `objectDate`, `medium`,
  `department` and `objectURL`. `classification` decides whether two
  records can be the same print.

  Worth trying other ids for the quirks the app absorbs:

  - `544502`: `"constituents": null` where a list is documented.
  - `57805`: `"tags": null`, and 12 `additionalImages`.
  - `dimensionsParsed` is documented and is in none of them.
}
